# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.
# Each ending is one carrier clause (the fleet's hail vote) times one arrival clause
# (the storm vote: held the plan, waited it out in orbit, or no storm). Every ending
# closes on the first crate. `title` is the heading; see STORY_BIBLE.md.

card end_lights
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Lights On
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_hold
text The storm left only a pre-dawn landing slot. Seven ships stand on the flat, three kilometres short of a glow. At midnight the flight director cleared one more command, lights only, and {A} sent it. At two kilometres up the dust turned white from below: Cargo 2, spending the battery it had saved on every floodlight. Seven pilots, blind in their plumes, checked radar against one glow. {B} set down closest. By dawn the glow is one lamp. At noon {B} is watching when it goes out. The first crate says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. The eighth kept the lights on." From a loading bay: "Told them it sulks."

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Through the Dust
when flag arrive_hold
text {B}'s ship is the one the gust caught. It stands on the slope three kilometres from Cargo 2, a strut folded under it: it will not fly home. {B} sits on the bottom rung, then starts a list of what it can still be: habitat, store, radio mast. Two sols later {A}, who wanted to answer from the start, climbs the rim with a battery pack. At two hundred metres {A} answers inside the tick, then the HOLD off the card on the next. HELLO RX · OK. The strobe goes out; one lamp burns steady. {B} adds a line to the list: neighbour. To Starbase: "Landed. Seven down, six to fly. Found the eighth." From a loading bay: "Tell it the bay says hello."

card end_long_orbit
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B wait_who
title The Long Orbit
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_wait
text Week three in the long orbit, half rations on seven galley tables. Below, the storm, and one lamp, steady since the handshake; the storm starves the wing. Its manifest comes a line a pass. Tonight: tank liners, a glove, a drill bit. Seven hungry people cheer a drill bit. Next pass: seed stock, frozen in week two. The budget held a lamp or a hold heater, not both, and the fleet asked for the lamp. {B}, who argued to wait, logs it. When the storm clears, {B} flies first, the lamp in the window, calling the numbers for six. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. The eighth was waiting." From a loading bay: "Thank it for the drill bit."

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Patience
when flag arrive_wait
text Dawn on the rim, frost on the wing. The long orbit is over: by last night all seven ships were down. For two weeks, longer than any chart gave it, a battery under that frost has been choosing which knock to skip, and the strobe has been dark since midnight. {A} kneels at the service port with a battery pack and a radio, {B} a step behind, counting. Clip, latch, wait. Nine. Ten. Eleven. A click, slow, like something clearing its throat. The answer goes in by hand, from two metres, inside the tick, and the HOLD after it. HELLO RX · OK. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. Found the eighth." From a loading bay: "Knew it'd keep."

card end_friend
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Sit With It
when flag signal_answered
text Second sol, halfway out, {A} driving, {B} on the battery: forty-eight percent used, and the reserve rule says turn round here. There and back is past the rover's range, unless Cargo 2's leg still charges a truck. The waiver takes sixteen minutes and says YOUR CALL. {A} drives on. Cargo 2 hears the rover and lights its floods and the charge port on its leg. Over the port, in marker: "Slow charger. Sit with it." {B} plugs in at four percent. They sit with it all afternoon, on the charge it kept for the cold. That night its lamp is dimmer, and stays that way. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight." From a loading bay: "Told you it was slow."

card end_close
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Close Enough
text Third sol, two hundred metres from Cargo 2, {A} and {B} in the cab. On the first sol Cargo 3's drill snapped its only bit; the spare is in that hold. The rover's spare batteries went to heaters on the second night. {A} counts the dark, nine, ten, eleven, and answers. HELLO RX · OK. The cargo doors unlatch. Cargo 2 obeys its patch, WAKE ALL: every heater at once, no battery check. The HOLD goes on the next tick, a tick it is no longer awake for. The strobe goes out for good. They drive back heaters off, the bit in {B}'s lap. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. Found the eighth, in time." From a loading bay: "Told them. Thank it for us."

